 "notes": "Generated by tools/mapgen-shoals.py from a 256-hex seed. Point-symmetric (mirror \"rot\": every op, prop and pad is copied rotated 180 degrees about the centre). West keep is a raised walled island with cliffs (drop off, can't climb) and gates N, S and E. The tidal flats (\"tide\" cells) are dry and fast for 40s, then flood to slow ford for 30s. Each team owns a stone causeway on its own flank (west: north, east: south) across a deep channel to an islet with a forward pad; the other team can only cross that channel on its enemy's causeway. Deep channels split the flats into a pinwheel; the drowned shrine islet in the centre holds the Grudge.",
